WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.684 --> 00:00:10.184
Ask an SI system a question, and the answer feels weightless. It isn't.

2
00:00:10.564 --> 00:00:18.984
It starts with power. Data centers the size of warehouses need enormous amounts of electricity, and cooling.

3
00:00:19.871 --> 00:00:24.824
Inside are the chips, from companies like Nvidia, AMD and Broadcom.

4
00:00:25.244 --> 00:00:29.004
Those chips need fast memory, from makers like Micron, and

5
00:00:29.004 --> 00:00:31.624
networks that link thousands of them together.

6
00:00:32.004 --> 00:00:36.004
Cloud companies, like Microsoft, Amazon and Google, rent that

7
00:00:36.004 --> 00:00:38.324
computing power to the world.

8
00:00:38.324 --> 00:00:46.084
On top run the frontier models, from labs like OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Meta and xAI.

9
00:00:46.084 --> 00:00:50.144
And all of it has to be secured against attackers.

10
00:00:50.144 --> 00:00:53.484
At the lunch, the President said communities that host data

11
00:00:53.484 --> 00:00:55.844
centers should benefit directly.

12
00:00:55.844 --> 00:01:01.464
That's why the guest list looked the way it did. The whole supply chain, in one room.
